Day 50/100 of #DrGVishwanathanChallenge
Today I solved LeetCode 100 -(Same Tree) 

- Approach:
I used recursion with DFS to compare the two binary trees:
If both nodes are null, they are identical at that position.
If one node is null or their values are different, the trees are not the same.
Recursively compare both the left subtrees and right subtrees.
The trees are considered the same only when both subtrees match at every level.

-Time Complexity:
O(n) -Each corresponding node is visited once.
-Space Complexity:
O(h)- Due to the recursive call stack, where h is the height of the tree.
Worst case: O(n) for a skewed tree.

Today's problem strengthened my understanding of Binary Trees, DFS, recursion, and base cases. It also reinforced how important it is to carefully handle null nodes when comparing tree structures.
